{
  "dom_id": "step-q237486",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/e4fb4cd078511a6fc3c7bcad2d82d5d8c5e57b72668c0f9bdd5f9fd2633ddce9.png)\n\nUse the model above to determine the missing number in the following division problem. \n\n$$\n2÷\\boxed{\\,\\,}=4\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by interpreting our model:\n\n- The model shows $2$ wholes. Each whole is split into *eighths*.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/5736ab37b8da1524868d18258fcbac73e216786d624b6e2f6c19f4be15f47761.png)\n\n \n\n- The eighths are grouped, and each group contains $\\frac{4}{8}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/1db3a2eea2b8ac696e49eee7262770627e472f83878cc6b61f830ea7dcc826f0.png)\n\n \n\n- There are $4$ groups in total.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/4dba3b1064014e57b98fc53443d82ed503fb2b87172c00603982ebe78408080f.png)\n\n \n\nSo, if we divide $2$ wholes into groups of $\\frac{4}{8},$ we get $4$ groups in total.\n\nTherefore, the model represents the following division problem:\n\n$$\n2÷\\boxed{\\frac{4}{8}}=4\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\frac{4}{8}.$",
